# The lookout's two tile layers. The map is `Map0010.json`: a slab of
# grass in the night sky, `Stars`, which does not move, and a parallel
# page that swaps it for `Dawn` with `ChangePBG` half a second after
# arriving. `tests/test_panorama_swap.py` says what is tested. And a
# dispatcher, an automatic page on switch 1430 that sends the hero to the
# clearing: `tests/test_jumps.py`.
#
# The sky is the transparent lower tile, as on the terrace; nothing is
# drawn above the hero, so the panorama goes on BG2 in mode 3 and is not
# flattened.

# 20x15, 300 tiles per layer
# The two tile layers, in reading order: one id per tile, 20 per line.
# These are the ids the binary stores; what turns them into pictures is
# the chipset. Edited by hand, the count has to stay the same.
